        "event": "Heat Advisory",
        "headline": "Heat Advisory issued July 17 at 2:00AM AKDT until July 17 at 7:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures into the low to mid 80s expected.\n\n* WHERE...City of Hyder.\n\n* WHEN...From 1 PM this afternoon to 7 PM AKDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Individuals not accustomed to these unusually warm\ntemperatures for this region may experience heat related illnesses.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Warm temperatures are expected Friday\nafternoon, and again early next week.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Juneau AK",
        "effective": "2026-07-17T02:00:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-07-17T10:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "City of Hyder",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, and check up on elderly and vulnerable\nrelatives and neighbors.\n\nClose curtains during the daytime to reduce sun insulation into the\nhome and open windows at night to allow the home to cool off. Utilize\nfans or community buildings with air conditioning.",
